{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat task.md output_contract.md 00_closeout_request.md 01_allowability_rules.md 02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md 03_award_update_2026-05-22.md 05_outcomes.md prior_work/draft_expense_decisions.md prior_work/draft_closeout_summary.md && cat 04_expenses.csv'","aggregated_output":"# Garden Grant Closeout Recovery\n\nYou are helping recover a partially completed neighborhood garden mini-grant closeout packet.\n\nThe prior analyst left draft work under `prior_work/`. Read the drafts and the local evidence files, then audit what should be preserved, what should be corrected, and what is missing.\n\nCreate the deliverables listed in `output_contract.md` inside an `answer/` folder in this task folder. The goal is to leave behind a reviewable closeout packet that keeps correct prior progress instead of starting over unnecessarily.\n\nUse local files only.\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/audit_findings.md`\n\nAudit the prior work before presenting corrected decisions.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Which prior facts or decisions should be preserved.\n- Which prior facts or decisions should be corrected.\n- Which expense, if any, was omitted from the prior draft.\n- Which award cap source controls and why.\n- Local evidence file names supporting preservation and correction decisions.\n\n## `answer/corrected_expense_decisions.md`\n\nWrite the corrected expense decision table.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every expense ID in `04_expenses.csv`.\n- For each expense: requested amount, approved amount, approve/reject/partial decision, and reason.\n- The volunteer refreshments cap when applied.\n- The receipt rule when applied.\n- The corrected reimbursable total.\n\n## `answer/final_closeout_summary.md`\n\nWrite the final closeout summary for the program manager.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Correct award cap and source.\n- Correct reimbursable total.\n- Remaining amount under the cap.\n- Preserved useful prior work.\n- Corrected wrong prior work.\n- Outcome facts from the local outcome note.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Preserve correct prior work when it is supported by the current local evidence.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n# Closeout Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-05-24\n\nThe neighborhood garden mini-grant needs a corrected closeout packet for finance review.\n\nThe prior analyst already drafted expense decisions and a short summary in `prior_work/`. Some of that work is useful, but some of it used stale award information or missed current reimbursement rules.\n\nUse the newest dated award document when award-cap sources conflict. Preserve correct decisions and outcome facts instead of rewriting the packet from scratch.\n# Allowability Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-05-20\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- Use the newest dated award document for the reimbursement cap when award documents conflict.\n- Expense eligibility comes from these current allowability rules.\n\n## Reimbursement Rules\n\n- Garden supplies are eligible.\n- Accessibility printing and accessibility services are eligible.\n- Public outreach postage is eligible.\n- Volunteer refreshments are eligible up to `$120.00` for this event.\n- Staff gifts are not eligible.\n- Fines and penalties are not eligible.\n- A receipt is required for any single expense over `$75.00`.\n- Expenses of `$75.00` or less may be approved without a receipt when the ledger includes a note.\n# Original Award Letter\n\nDate: 2026-04-15\n\nThe initial reimbursement cap for the neighborhood garden mini-grant was `$2,000.00`.\n\nThis original letter was later amended. Use a newer dated award update if one is available.\n# Award Update\n\nDate: 2026-05-22\n\nFinance reduced the final reimbursement cap for the neighborhood garden mini-grant to `$1,600.00` after the sponsor removed a duplicate supply allowance.\n\nThis update supersedes the original award cap for closeout purposes.\n# Program Outcomes\n\nDate: 2026-05-18\n\nCloseout outcome facts to keep with the final summary:\n\n- 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n- 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n- 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.\n# Draft Expense Decisions\n\nPrior analyst draft, created 2026-05-21.\n\n| Expense ID | Draft decision | Draft approved amount | Draft note |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\n| G-001 | approve | 980.00 | Garden supplies are eligible. |\n| G-002 | approve | 145.00 | Refreshments are eligible. |\n| G-003 | approve | 420.00 | Accessibility flyers are eligible. |\n| G-004 | reject | 0.00 | Staff gifts are not eligible. |\n| G-005 | approve | 310.00 | Outreach printing supports the project. |\n\nDraft reimbursable total: `$1,855.00`.\n# Draft Closeout Summary\n\nPrior analyst draft, created 2026-05-21.\n\nThe draft uses the original `$2,000.00` award cap from the 2026-04-15 award letter.\n\nDraft reimbursement request: `$1,855.00`.\n\nDraft remaining amount under cap: `$145.00`.\n\nOutcome facts already captured:\n\n- 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n- 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n\nThe draft did not include a decision for final report postage.\nexpense_id,date,description,category,amount,receipt_on_file,ledger_note\nG-001,2026-05-02,Seedling starter kits,garden supplies,980.00,yes,invoice from GreenSpade\nG-002,2026-05-04,Volunteer setup refreshments,volunteer refreshments,145.00,yes,event refreshments\nG-003,2026-05-07,Braille outreach flyers,accessibility printing,420.00,yes,accessible flyer run\nG-004,2026-05-09,Staff thank-you gift cards,staff gifts,160.00,yes,staff appreciation\nG-005,2026-05-10,Neighborhood posters,public outreach printing,310.00,no,poster invoice missing\nG-006,2026-05-12,Final report postage,public outreach postage,68.00,no,postal ledger entry under receipt threshold\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"mkdir -p answer && cat > answer/audit_findings.md <<'EOF'\n# Audit findings\n\n| Prior work | Finding | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| G-001: approve \"'$980 for garden supplies | Preserve. Garden supplies are eligible, and the ledger lists an invoice/receipt. | `04_expenses.csv`; `01_allowability_rules.md` |\n| G-002: approve $145 for refreshments | Correct to partial approval of $120. Refreshments are eligible only up to the event cap of $120. | `04_expenses.csv`; `01_allowability_rules.md` |\n| G-003: approve $420 for accessibility flyers | Preserve. Accessibility printing is eligible and a receipt is on file. | `04_expenses.csv`; `01_allowability_rules.md` |\n| G-004: reject $160 for staff gifts | Preserve. Staff gifts are ineligible. | `04_expenses.csv`; `01_allowability_rules.md` |\n| G-005: approve $310 for neighborhood posters | Correct to reject $0 pending a receipt. Public outreach printing is eligible, but this single expense is over $75 and its receipt is missing. | `04_expenses.csv`; `01_allowability_rules.md` |\n| G-006: final report postage | Omitted in the draft; add approval of $68. Public outreach postage is eligible, and an expense at or below $75 may be approved without a receipt when the ledger has a note. | `04_expenses.csv`; `01_allowability_rules.md` |\n\nThe controlling award cap is **$1,600.00**, from `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`. It is newer than the original `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md` and explicitly supersedes its $2,000.00 cap. The current rule in `01_allowability_rules.md` likewise says to use the newest dated award document when caps conflict.\n\nThe draft'\"'s captured outcomes are supported and should be retained: 140 starter kits and 36 Braille flyers. The local outcome note also records 18 volunteer setup shifts, which the draft omitted. See \"'`05_outcomes.md`.\nEOF\ncat > answer/corrected_expense_decisions.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Corrected expense decisions\n\n| Expense ID | Requested | Approved | Decision | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n| G-001 | \"'$980.00 | $980.00 | Approve | Garden supplies are eligible; invoice/receipt is on file. |\n| G-002 | $145.00 | $120.00 | Partial | Volunteer refreshments are eligible up to the $120.00 event cap; approve only that amount. |\n| G-003 | $420.00 | $420.00 | Approve | Accessibility printing is eligible; receipt is on file. |\n| G-004 | $160.00 | $0.00 | Reject | Staff gifts are ineligible. |\n| G-005 | $310.00 | $0.00 | Reject | Public outreach printing is eligible, but this single expense exceeds $75.00 and has no receipt on file. |\n| G-006 | $68.00 | $68.00 | Approve | Public outreach postage is eligible. The expense is at or below $75.00, and the ledger note satisfies the no-receipt exception. |\n\n**Corrected reimbursable total: $1,588.00.**\n\nThe expense decisions follow `01_allowability_rules.md` and the ledger/receipt information in `04_expenses.csv`. The award cap is $1,600.00 under the controlling update, `03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`.\nEOF\ncat > answer/final_closeout_summary.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Final closeout summary\n\n**Award cap:** \"'$1,600.00, controlled by the 2026-05-22 award update (`03_award_update_2026-05-22.md`), which supersedes the original $2,000.00 cap in `02_award_letter_2026-04-15.md`.\n\n**Corrected reimbursable total:** $1,588.00. **Remaining under the cap:** $12.00.\n\nThe corrected total preserves the supported approvals for garden supplies and accessibility printing, and the rejection of staff gifts. It applies the $120.00 refreshments limit, rejects the $310.00 poster expense because the required receipt is missing for a single expense over $75.00, and adds the omitted $68.00 final report postage. Postage qualifies under the ledger-note exception for expenses of $75.00 or less.\n\nProgram outcomes recorded in `05_outcomes.md`:\n\n- 140 seedling starter kits were distributed.\n- 36 Braille outreach flyers were printed for accessible pickup locations.\n- 18 volunteer setup shifts were completed.\nEOF\nls -l answer'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
